cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this code, please cite the preprint below (arXiv:2607.22077).
title: "STSF-TPLS: image-free single-pixel segmentation"
abstract: >-
  Official implementation of an image-free single-pixel segmentation framework:
  a spatiotemporal soft-fusion network (STSF) with a content-adaptive
  measurement-to-space lift, trained under a task-prioritized loss schedule
  (TPLS). The network predicts a segmentation mask directly from a 1D
  single-pixel measurement sequence, without reconstructing an intermediate
  image.
authors:
  - family-names: Han
    given-names: Yuyuan
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Hanyuyuan6/STSF-TPLS"
keywords:
  - single-pixel imaging
  - image-free sensing
  - image segmentation
  - computational imaging
  - ghost imaging
  - compressed sensing
  - deep learning
  - pytorch
